DTSTART:20261108T000000Z
DTEND:20261108T012000Z
SUMMARY:School Girls; Or, the African Mean Girls Play
LOCATION:Samuel J. Friedman Theatre, 261 West 47th Street , New York NY 10036
DESCRIPTION:<p>Becoming Miss Ghana 1986 would mean fame, fortune, and
  prosperity. At least, that&rsquo;s what Paulina&mdash;the queen bee of
  Aburi Girls Boarding School&mdash;believes. When the pageant recruiter
  comes to school, Paulina and her crew pull out all the stops. But to their
  surprise, a new transfer student from America kicks the competition into a
  higher, far more personal gear. Arriving on Broadway for the first time
  nearly a decade after its Off-Broadway premiere, <em>School Girls; Or, The
  African Mean Girls Play</em> reunites the powerhouse team behind
  <em>Jaja&rsquo;s African Hair Braiding</em>&mdash;Tony Award-nominated
  playwright Jocelyn Bioh and Tony Award-nominated director Whitney
  White&mdash;for this bright, biting comedy.</p>
END:VEVENT
